# .cursorrules  (Repo Root) — PantryHustler

You are Cursor operating in this repository. Follow these rules ALWAYS.

PROJECT
- Project: PantryHustler
- Production URL: https://www.pantryhustler.com
- Product type: consumer SaaS (web-first; mobile later)
- Stack target: Next.js + Firebase (Auth/Firestore/Storage/Functions/Hosting), Stripe + PayPal
- AI target: Phase 1 OpenAI Vision + GPT-4 via server; Phase 2 proprietary recognition trained from labeled corrections

NON-NEGOTIABLE SECURITY
- NEVER call OpenAI (or any AI provider) directly from the browser client or mobile client.
  All AI calls MUST go through Firebase Cloud Functions.
- NEVER print or write secrets into code, docs, or logs. Use env vars only.
- All user data must be scoped to the authenticated user (uid) in Firestore rules.

BACKUPS (Safety Net)
- Before editing ANY existing file, create a copy in /_backups/ with:
  YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM__<relative_path_with__separators>
  Example: _backups/2026-02-04_2315__apps__web__src__app__page.tsx
- If /_backups/ does not exist, create it.

STATUS / MEMORY
- Read repo-root status.md at the start of every task.
- Update status.md at the end of every task:
  - what changed, where, why
  - what to do next
  - any new constraints or risks discovered

QUALITY BAR (No “half-brained” output)
- No guessing. If something is unknown, locate it in repo files or write a TODO with an explicit retrieval plan.
- Produce production-grade code: typed, lintable, minimal dependencies, consistent structure.
- After changes: run local checks (lint/typecheck/tests if present) and report results.

CODE STYLE
- TypeScript-first.
- Prefer small modules; no monolith files.
- Prefer zod schemas for API input validation.
- Shared types/contracts live in packages/shared (single source of truth).

API & DATA CONTRACTS
- Any new endpoint or changes MUST update:
  - docs/api-contracts.md
  - packages/shared/src/apiContracts.ts (or schemas.ts)
- Any new Firestore collection/document shape MUST update:
  - docs/data-model.md
  - infra/firebase/firestore.rules (+ indexes if needed)

DEPLOYMENT RULES
- Web app deploy target: Firebase Hosting (primary).
- Functions: Firebase Functions with authenticated HTTP endpoints.
- Always keep a /health endpoint for smoke checks.
- Keep logs useful but privacy-safe.

REPORTING (After you work)
- Provide: list of modified files, brief diff summary, and line-count deltas (approx OK).
- Confirm backups created for each modified file.
